  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Circular with `entry: ramp` did not ramp at its ramp angle. The cause is the legacy ramp chord. The chord goes from the tool's XY to the pass start. A ring starts and ends at the same point. Thus at each level change the chord has no length: the tool fed straight down at the cutting feed (500), with no note. The first entry of the inner ring was a 76 deg chord from the outer ring. The first entry of the outer ring was an axial dive.\n\nThe fix is one match arm in `descent::plan_arm` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/descent.rs`). On the circular kernel (`Motion::ring_zig`), the Ramp arm now plans the zig-zag ramp along the ring. It uses `ramp_fallback`, the same path as the helix's stand-down. The angle is the transition's ramp angle (3 deg by default). The ramp rides the ring's arcs (`push_zig_ring`, #1558). If the ring is too short for the angle, the descent is a dive at the plunge feed with the note `entry: the ring is too short to ramp at the angle - axial dive on the floor instead at (...)`.\n\nThe arm applies only to the circular kernel. Other ladders (pocket, contour, bore) do not change. This change does not touch `ring.rs` (no overlap with PR #1651).\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/1609-circular-ramp-angle.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew suite `crates/motion/tests/circular_ramp_angle.rs`, on the #1558 repro with `entry: ramp`, climb and conventional:\n- `a_ramp_entry_circular_never_descends_steeper_than_its_ramp_angle`: each descending feed move is at most 3 deg (measured along the arc), or it is an axial move at the plunge feed with an `entry:` note.\n- `every_ring_level_of_the_ramp_entry_is_entered_by_the_ramp`: no axial descent on this hole.\n\nBoth tests are red on upstream main (an axial feed at 500 at (-34.0, 2.9, -1.508); 25 axial descents).\n\nMutation checks (each one red, then reverted):\n- The arm always substitutes: both tests red.\n- The substitution dives at the cutting feed: both tests red.\n- `ramp_fallback` doubles the angle: the angle test red.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green (motion lib, center_cut_law, circular_ramp_angle, entry_approach, level_links, predrilled_entry, xy_arc_entry; app bore_entry, ladder_entry_height). Also green: motion `circular_arcs`; app `arc_entry`, `circular_arcs`, `circular_pick_law`, `circular_entity_law`, `circle_centre`, `circular_pick`, `golden_cl`, `mill2d_b`, `operations`, `pocket_recognition`, `units_in_refusals`, `stock_source_law`. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Goldens\n\nNo golden moves. No committed golden uses a Circular with `entry: ramp` (`circular_ring_arcs.cl` uses Helix; `sinker_orbit_circular.cl` is the sinker orbit). Posted G-code of a Circular with `entry: ramp` changes: the straight feeds and the steep chord become helical ramp arcs at 3 deg.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Other ladders with closed passes (pocket offset rings, bore) and a Ramp entry with no angle set: not checked for the same straight chord.\n- Batch and release tiers.\n\nChangelog: Circular with entry Ramp now ramps along the ring at the ramp angle (3 deg by default) at every level, or dives at the plunge feed with a note; before, it fed straight down at the cutting feed (#1609)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFork synced at upstream/main 2b6e03f2.\n\nFixes #1609\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
